WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:15.480
<v Ira Glass>It's OK to say this, right? There's a lot of long-term joy to being a parent. But the daily job of it, the mundane feeding your kids and driving them around and disciplining them-- there's not always a lot of pleasure in that.
<v Ira Glass>这样说应该没问题吧？为人父母有着许多长久的快乐。但其中的日常工作，那些琐事，比如喂孩子、开车送他们去这儿去那儿、管教他们——这些过程中并不总是充满乐趣。

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:33.440
<v Ira Glass>Which is why, whenever I've talked to Elna Baker about her parents-- Elna works here at the radio show-- whenever Elna talks about her parents, I've always been so impressed at the happy originality of some of their parenting moves, like the ingenuity that her dad brought to tasks that no parent enjoys.
<v Ira Glass>正因如此，每当我跟埃尔娜·贝克谈起她的父母——埃尔娜就在我们这档广播节目工作——每当埃尔娜提到她的父母，我总是对他们育儿方式中那种快乐的原创性印象深刻，比如她父亲在处理那些没哪个家长会喜欢的任务时，所展现出的独创性。

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:43.800
<v Ira Glass>For instance, let's say he would discover that one of the kids had broken something, or eaten a piece of cake that nobody was supposed to touch. He would gather the kids together.
<v Ira Glass>比如说，假设他发现孩子们中间有谁打破了东西，或者偷吃了谁都不该碰的蛋糕。他会把孩子们召集到一起。

00:00:43.800 --> 00:01:03.500
<v Elna Baker>So with five kids, he would ask all of us which one of us had done it, and we would all lie. And so his way of determining who really did it was he would say, line up, tallest to shortest-- he would always make us line up tallest to shortest. I don't know, I think he saw Sound of Music . And if you have five kids, why not?
<v Elna Baker>因为有五个孩子，他会问我们是谁干的，我们都会撒谎。而他判断谁才是真凶的方法是，他说：排好队，从最高到最矮——他总是让我们按从高到矮排队。我不知道，我想他大概是看过《音乐之声》。如果家里有五个孩子，为什么不呢？

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:03.820
<v Ira Glass>Yeah?
<v Ira Glass>是吗？

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:19.470
<v Elna Baker>So we would line up against the wall. And he said, I'm going to do the hot knife. And what he would do is he would take out like a butter knife. And he would hold a match or a lighter underneath it. And he would say stick out your tongues.
<v Elna Baker>所以我们就靠着墙排成一排。他说，我要用“热刀”。他拿出一把黄油刀，在下面点了一根火柴或打火机。然后他说：把舌头伸出来。

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:28.200
<v Elna Baker>And so if you're the liar, it'll burn your tongue, is what was explained to us. You're nervous, and all the saliva on your tongue will dry up.
<v Elna Baker>他解释说，如果你是撒谎者，刀就会烫伤你的舌头。你很紧张，舌头上的唾液会干掉。

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.470
<v Ira Glass>But if you're telling the truth--
<v Ira Glass>但如果你说的是实话——

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:36.800
<v Elna Baker>Then you'll have enough moisture on your tongue and it won't burn.
<v Elna Baker>那你的舌头就会保持湿润，就不会被烫伤。

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:48.680
<v Ira Glass>OK, of course, that's ridiculous. What was really happening was, he wouldn't hold the flame close enough to the knife to heat it up at all. So the knife wasn't hot, and then he would put the knife on the tongue of his oldest daughter.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，当然，这很荒谬。实际上发生的情况是，他并没有把火焰靠得离刀太近，根本没加热。所以刀一点都不烫，然后他把刀贴在大女儿的舌头上。

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:56.540
<v Elna Baker>And so she would be the first. And by the time he went to move on to me, the second child, one of us would confess.
<v Elna Baker>她是第一个。等他轮到我这个第二个孩子时，我们中就会有人招认了。

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:57.520
<v Elna Baker>[LAUGHTER]
<v Elna Baker>[笑声]

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:06.650
<v Elna Baker>One of us would be like, I did it. I couldn't help it. I'm so sorry.
<v Elna Baker>我们中会有人说，是我干的。我忍不住了。真的非常抱歉。

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:20.740
<v Ira Glass>So Elna's dad definitely tried to do the right thing as a parent. But he didn't mind entertaining himself in the process. And occasionally, he would ad hoc his way to moves that had a secret kind of long-term genius to them that took years to pay off.
<v Ira Glass>所以埃尔娜的父亲作为一名家长，确实努力在做正确的事。但他也不介意在此过程中给自己找点乐子。偶尔，他会即兴想出一些带有长期天才色彩的妙招，只是需要多年时间才能显现出成效。

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:32.330
<v Ira Glass>Like, for example, the day Elna hit her sister on the head with a broom. That day began with Elna's parents sending all five kids out to clean up the garage, which her parents would do now and then.
<v Ira Glass>比如，埃尔娜有次用扫帚打了她妹妹的头。那天开始于埃尔娜的父母让五个孩子去清理车库，这是他们偶尔会做的事。

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:42.820
<v Elna Baker>I think we thought we were doing real cleaning, but mostly they just wanted to spend some alone time with the kids not in the house. They would make up either outdoor chores or the garage.
<v Elna Baker>我想我们当时以为自己在做真正的清洁工作，但其实他们主要是想找点私人时间，不想让孩子在屋里。他们要么会编造出户外杂活，要么就让我们去打扫车库。

00:02:42.820 --> 00:03:01.380
<v Ira Glass>Elna's little sister Julia found a pair of skates in the garage and she was just skating around, which annoyed Elna, who was really trying to work and clean the garage. Elna was nine, Julia was five. Elna told Julia to get to work. Elna was ignored, which in her mind was not how things were supposed to go between her and her little sister.
<v Ira Glass>埃尔娜的小妹妹朱莉娅在车库里发现了一双溜冰鞋，就在那儿滑来滑去，这惹恼了正努力打扫车库的埃尔娜。埃尔娜九岁，朱莉娅五岁。埃尔娜叫朱莉娅去干活。朱莉娅无视了她，这在埃尔娜看来，绝不是她和妹妹之间该有的相处方式。

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:18.630
<v Ira Glass>And she got so mad that she took this broom-- and it was one of those big industrial booms with the big, heavy, wide tops-- and she bashed Julia with it, bashed her in the head. Blood pours down Julia's face. Elena suddenly realizes, like, oh my god, this is serious. What did I do?
<v Ira Glass>她气急败坏地拿起了那把扫帚——那种带有巨大、沉重、宽阔扫头的工业扫帚——狠狠地砸向朱莉娅，砸在了她的头上。鲜血顺着朱莉娅的脸流了下来。埃尔娜突然意识到，天哪，这事儿严重了。我做了什么？

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:30.620
<v Elna Baker>It wasn't like a line-- it was like a stream of blood came running down her head. And I genuinely thought I had maybe, accidentally killed my sister.
<v Elna Baker>那不是一道痕迹，而是一股血流顺着她的头流了下来。我当时真的以为我可能不小心把妹妹杀死了。

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.360
<v Ira Glass>Julia runs to their dad, who administers first aid.
<v Ira Glass>朱莉娅跑向他们的父亲，父亲为她进行了急救。

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:40.760
<v Elna Baker>And I remember just watching from the corner of the bathroom, just towels of blood from the top of her head.
<v Elna Baker>我记得我当时躲在浴室角落里看着，满是鲜血的毛巾从她头顶拿下来。

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:54.790
<v Ira Glass>Once the bleeding stops, and Julia's bandaged up, Elna's dad comes out into the hallway, and he asks Elna, what happened? Elna knows how much trouble she would be in if she admitted the truth, so she lies. She says it was an accident-- the broom slipped.
<v Ira Glass>血止住后，朱莉娅包扎好了，埃尔娜的父亲来到走廊，问埃尔娜发生了什么事。埃尔娜知道如果承认真相会惹多大麻烦，于是她撒谎了。她说是个意外——扫帚滑了一下。

00:03:54.790 --> 00:04:02.330
<v Elna Baker>I remember him saying, are you sure that's what happened? And I said yes.
<v Elna Baker>我记得他说，你确定是这样吗？我说确定。

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:15.800
<v Ira Glass>Julia, of course, had told him what really happened-- that Elna walloped her intentionally. And now Elena's dad was in the annoying situation that parents find themselves in now and then. One child says it happened one way, one says the opposite. And he gets an idea.
<v Ira Glass>当然，朱莉娅已经告诉了他真相——埃尔娜是故意狠狠揍了她。现在埃尔娜的父亲陷入了家长们偶尔会遇到的那种烦人处境。一个孩子说是一种情况，另一个说完全相反。然后他想到了一个主意。

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:29.490
<v Elna Baker>So he brought everyone in. We all sat on my parents' bed. And he proceeded to conduct a family trial, where each child had to give their testimony of the events in the garage.
<v Elna Baker>于是他把所有人都叫了进去。我们都坐在父母的床上。他开始主持一场家庭审判，让每个孩子都要陈述在车库里发生的事。

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.830
<v Ira Glass>And he videotaped this?
<v Ira Glass>他还录像了？

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:31.880
<v Elna Baker>Yes.
<v Elna Baker>是的。

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:43.340
<v Ira Glass>That's right. There's video of this. They had just gotten their first video camera. And her dad thought, oh, maybe this is the kind of thing you use this for. Or who knows, maybe he just thought the camera added gravitas to the proceedings.
<v Ira Glass>没错。有这段录像。他们当时刚买了第一台摄像机。她父亲想，噢，也许这就是这种东西的用途。或者谁知道呢，也许他只是觉得摄像机增加了审讯的严肃感。

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:49.770
<v Julia>We were cleaning outside, and I was [INAUDIBLE].
<v Julia>我们在外面打扫，我当时……[听不清]。

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:59.570
<v Ira Glass>OK, so there's this shot here of your little sister. She looks like she's been crying, and she's about to burst into tears more any second. Like, her eyes are big and wide and watery.
<v Ira Glass>好的，画面里有你小妹妹的镜头。她看起来刚哭过，随时都可能又要大哭一场。她的眼睛睁得大大的，眼眶湿润。

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:05.950
<v Elna Baker>Her hair is wet from the blood, and she has a bandage in the center of her head.
<v Elna Baker>她的头发被血弄湿了，头顶中间贴着一块绷带。

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:12.270
<v Ira Glass>The bandage is like a comic prop. It's just a Band-Aid, a regular Band-Aid, stuck to her hair.
<v Ira Glass>那块绷带就像滑稽道具。那只是个创可贴，普通的创可贴，粘在头发上。

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:20.530
<v Julia>And then Elna holded the handle up high, and then it went down.
<v Julia>然后埃尔娜把柄举得很高，然后它就掉下来了。

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:22.560
<v Gary Baker>So was it Elna's fault?
<v Gary Baker>所以是埃尔娜的错吗？

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.470
<v Julia>Yes.
<v Julia>是的。

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.100
<v Gary Baker>She did it on purpose?
<v Gary Baker>她是故意的吗？

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.520
<v Julia>Yeah.
<v Julia>是的。

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.970
<v Gary Baker>OK, Elna, what's your story?
<v Gary Baker>好的，埃尔娜，你的版本是什么？

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:34.670
<v Child Elna>I just told you. Well, I didn't do that on purpose. I was just holding it.
<v Child Elna>我刚才已经说了。嗯，我不是故意的。我只是拿着它而已。

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:40.450
<v Ira Glass>All right. Now I just want to describe the way you look in this. First of all, you have a huge smile on your face.
<v Ira Glass>好了。现在我想描述一下你在这段录像里的样子。首先，你脸上挂着一个巨大的微笑。

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:44.780
<v Elna Baker>Yeah. I'm trying to play it super casual.
<v Elna Baker>是的。我当时正努力装得非常随意。

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:55.570
<v Child Elna>I asked Julia to come and help me get all the stuff out of the thingamajigger. And then she accidentally got hit with the broom, the side of it--
<v Child Elna>我叫朱莉娅来帮我把杂物从那个玩意儿里拿出来。然后她不小心被扫帚扫到了，扫帚侧面——

00:05:55.570 --> 00:06:02.340
<v Ira Glass>I'm just going to note that you never meet your dad's eye, you never look up at the camera, you're totally avoiding everyone's gaze.
<v Ira Glass>我要指出的是，你始终没有看向父亲的眼睛，也没有看镜头，你完全是在回避所有人的目光。

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:14.440
<v Child Elna>And she started crying, and I went over by the car and I said, it's all right. You're going to be OK. And I hugged her and I looked at her head, and I took her inside, and dad fixed her all up.
<v Child Elna>然后她开始哭，我走过去靠在车边说，没事的。你会没事的。我抱了她，看了看她的头，然后把她带进屋，爸爸就给她处理好了。

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:28.310
<v Ira Glass>Elna's dad pulls the other kids as witnesses. Elna's older sister didn't actually see anything, but concludes in the testimony that Elna probably did not mean to hit Julia so hard, but probably did hit her, which actually seems like the truth of the situation.
<v Ira Glass>埃尔娜的父亲叫来其他孩子作证。埃尔娜的姐姐其实没看见什么，但在证词中总结说埃尔娜可能并不是故意打那么重，但很可能确实打了她，这看起来似乎就是事实真相。

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:35.230
<v Ira Glass>Elna's dad turns back to Elna after each bit of testimony, and Elna's voice gets higher and higher as she holds on to her lie.
<v Ira Glass>每次听完证词，埃尔娜的父亲都转回身问埃尔娜，而埃尔娜的声音因为坚持撒谎而变得越来越尖。

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:40.840
<v Child Elna>And the broom accidentally slipped, and it accidentally hit her on the head, and I didn't do that on purpose.
<v Child Elna>扫帚不小心滑了，不小心打到了她的头，我不是故意的。

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:50.090
<v Ira Glass>Can I just say, if there are any little kids listening to the program today-- seriously, learn from this. Listen to how high Elna's voice gets when she says, no, I didn't.
<v Ira Glass>我能说一句吗，如果今天节目有小孩子在听——认真点，从中学到教训。听听埃尔娜在说“不，我没有”时声音有多高。

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:53.640
<v Gary Baker>Do you believe she did it on purpose?
<v Gary Baker>你相信她是故意的吗？

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.540
<v Julia>She did it on purpose.
<v Julia>她是故意的。

00:06:55.540 --> 00:07:00.670
<v Child Elna>I didn't.
<v Child Elna>我没有。

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:17.360
<v Ira Glass>The dad moves into the sentencing part of the trial, asks Julia what punishment would be fair. Julia thinks spanking. And it feels like that is where this is headed. Elna's dad turns to her mom to administer the punishment, and then her mom just turns everything upside down when she says--
<v Ira Glass>父亲进入了审判的判决环节，问朱莉娅什么样的惩罚才公平。朱莉娅觉得应该打屁股。感觉事情就要往那方向发展了。埃尔娜的父亲转向母亲去执行惩罚，然后母亲的一句话让一切峰回路转——

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.990
<v Mrs. Baker>I'm not convinced that it was on purpose.
<v Mrs. Baker>我不相信她是故意的。

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:20.880
<v Gary Baker>Oh, you're not?
<v Gary Baker>噢，不相信吗？

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.400
<v Mrs. Baker>No, because if you think about it--
<v Mrs. Baker>不，因为如果你仔细想的话——

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:30.130
<v Ira Glass>She says, the way Elna was holding the broom, it really could have been an accident. It's stupid to hold a broom with the heavy part in the  air, she says.
<v Ira Glass>她说，以埃尔娜拿扫帚的方式，那确实可能是个意外。她说，拿着重的一头举在空中是很蠢的。

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:34.310
<v Gary Baker>So the only thing Elna's guilty of is stupidity?
<v Gary Baker>所以埃尔娜唯一的罪过就是愚蠢？

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.740
<v Mrs. Baker>Yeah.
<v Mrs. Baker>是的。

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.690
<v Gary Baker>Elna, what do you think of that?
<v Gary Baker>埃尔娜，你觉得呢？

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:54.720
<v Elna Baker>It pans from my mom to me, and you see that I've just taken in that I might get off. And I have this-- I go from this moment of where I was just almost crying, and I have this really mischievous smile on my face and I say, I guess I'm stupid.
<v Elna Baker>镜头从我妈妈转向我，你可以看到我意识到自己可能逃脱惩罚后的表情。我从刚才那个几乎要哭的状态，脸上露出了一种非常顽皮的笑容，我说，我想我是挺蠢的。

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:01.430
<v Child Elna>I guess I'm stupid.
<v Child Elna>我想我是挺蠢的。

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:13.680
<v Ira Glass>And with that, she gets off. No spanking, no consequences. And then, Elna says, a funny thing happened. It just stuck with her. Wouldn't go away.
<v Ira Glass>就这样，她脱身了。没有打屁股，没有任何后果。然后，埃尔娜说，一件有趣的事情发生了。它一直困扰着她，挥之不去。

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:32.880
<v Elna Baker>I thought about it way more than if I'd just been spanked. I carried the guilt of this for most of my childhood. Like in church, when they would talk about lying or sin, this is the thing I would hold onto and relive, because it was the worst thing I'd ever done.
<v Elna Baker>我思考它的次数比直接挨打要多得多。我在整个童年时期都背负着这种愧疚感。比如在教堂里，当他们谈论谎言或罪恶时，我就会想到并重温这件事，因为这是我做过的最糟糕的事。

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.710
<v Elna Baker>And then also feeling so much worse because I'd then lied about it, and gotten away with it.
<v Elna Baker>而且因为我后来撒了谎并且逃脱了惩罚，心里更难受了。

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:42.590
<v Ira Glass>Did you also worry that after you died that was going to keep you out of heaven?
<v Ira Glass>你有没有担心过，死后这会让你进不了天堂？

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:47.670
<v Elna Baker>Yeah, I did. Like I thought a part of me was evil because I was capable of doing it.
<v Elna Baker>是的，我担心过。我觉得自己有一部分是邪恶的，因为我竟然做得出来。

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:55.540
<v Ira Glass>Doing it of lying, she means. Of tricking her parents. It was a scheming, selfish part of her that seemed worse than just hitting her sister.
<v Ira Glass>“做得出来”，她是说撒谎这件事。欺骗父母这件事。那是她身上邪恶、自私的一面，这看起来比仅仅打了妹妹更严重。

00:08:55.540 --> 00:09:01.530
<v Elna Baker>And I was afraid of that part of me, because I got away with it.
<v Elna Baker>我害怕我身上的那一部分，因为我逃脱了惩罚。

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:04.390
<v Ira Glass>And then do you think it kept you from hitting her more?
<v Ira Glass>那你觉得这是否让你没有再打她了？

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:13.820
<v Elna Baker>Yeah, I never hit her again. I would want to hit her. I would clench my fist and make this face, but I never hit her.
<v Elna Baker>是的，我再也没打过她。我想过要打她。我会握紧拳头，做出那种表情，但我从没打过她。

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:27.500
<v Ira Glass>Not that she stopped being mean. She was still so mean to her sister. She told Julia she was stupid. She said mean things in front of her friends. She trained the baby in the family, Jill, to start crying if Julia ever picked up.
<v Ira Glass>并不是说她不再刻薄了。她对妹妹依然很刻薄。她对朱莉娅说她很蠢。她在朋友面前说刻薄的话。她甚至教家里的幼子吉尔，只要朱莉娅一抱他，就开始大哭。

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:43.700
<v Ira Glass>But Elna grew up remembering the trial. She did not remember it was videotaped, though. Then nearly 20 years after the event, her brother found the video in some old boxes. And they popped it in and they watched it together, as a family, with her parents and everybody.
<v Ira Glass>但埃尔娜长大后一直记着那次审判。不过，她当时并不知道过程被录了下来。近20年后，她哥哥在旧箱子里发现了录像带。全家人坐在一起看了，包括她父母。

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:52.190
<v Ira Glass>And to Elna's surprise-- OK, she thought, back when she was nine, she thought she was like a criminal mastermind or something to put this lie over on both of her parents.
<v Ira Glass>令埃尔娜惊讶的是——好吧，她当时九岁时，以为自己是个犯罪天才，能骗过父母双方。

00:09:52.190 --> 00:10:05.740
<v Elna Baker>And you watch it now as an adult, and I just think watching me, how could you possibly believe me? I'm so obviously lying. Obviously, I'm guilty. And I say to my dad, how on earth did you not think that I was guilty?
<v Elna Baker>而当你现在作为一个成年人去看它时，我看着当时的自己，觉得怎么可能相信我？我撒谎撒得太明显了。显然我有罪。我问父亲，你怎么可能一点都不觉得我有罪？

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:11.590
<v Elna Baker>And his response was, I knew you were guilty the second you walked in the house.
<v Elna Baker>他的回答是，你进屋的那一秒我就知道你有罪。

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:20.190
<v Gary Baker>I knew that she did it. You could just see her eyes just shifting back and forth, so you knew, or I knew, she's a little liar.
<v Gary Baker>我知道是她干的。你可以看到她的眼睛不停地左右闪烁，所以我知道，我知道，她是个小骗子。

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:32.340
<v Ira Glass>This, of course, is Elna's dad, Gary Baker. He told me that after she lied to him at the very beginning, he staged the trial, expecting that she would cave, she would do the right thing, she would tell the truth. And then she didn't.
<v Ira Glass>这就是埃尔娜的父亲，加里·贝克。他告诉我，在他最初审问时她撒谎后，他策划了那场审判，期望她会崩溃，会做正确的事，会说实话。但她没有。

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:41.730
<v Ira Glass>Her mom, by the way, told me she also was not convinced by Elna. She tried to push the idea that it was an accident for Julia's sake, so Julia wouldn't be so scared of Elna going forward.
<v Ira Glass>顺便说一下，她母亲告诉我，她当时也没被埃尔娜说服。她尝试提出意外的论点是为了朱莉娅好，这样朱莉娅以后就不会那么怕埃尔娜。

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:52.900
<v Ira Glass>But once she raised the possibility of not punishing Elna, her dad grabbed at the idea, and just made a judgment on the fly that that would be a more effective punishment for Elna, given Elna's personality.
<v Ira Glass>但一旦她提出了不惩罚埃尔娜的可能性，她父亲就抓住了这个点，临时做出了决定，考虑到埃尔娜的个性，这会对她更有效。

00:10:52.900 --> 00:11:06.960
<v Gary Baker>I decided that she's going to have to live with this. She knows that she did it. She knows that she hurt her little sister. She knows the truth. And so she's going to live with that for the rest of her life.
<v Gary Baker>我决定让她自己去承受。她知道是她干的。她知道她伤害了自己的小妹妹。她知道真相。所以她这辈子都得背负着这个真相生活下去。

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.310
<v Ira Glass>And you thought that would be better than just spanking her?
<v Ira Glass>你觉得这比打她一顿要好吗？

