<v Elna Baker>And this is what Julia says. I wonder why Elna is so mean to me. I wonder if anyone likes me. I wonder whether my sister loves me. I wonder how come Elna doesn't like me. I wonder where I could be happy.
<v Elna Baker>这是朱莉娅写的。我很好奇埃尔娜为什么对我那么刻薄。我很好奇是否有人喜欢我。我很好奇姐姐是否爱我。我很好奇为什么埃尔娜不喜欢我。我很好奇在哪里我才能快乐。

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:12.230
<v Ira Glass>You were awful.
<v Ira Glass>你当时真是太糟糕了。

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:31.130
<v Elna Baker>I was awful. And she read it-- the whole family, everyone was laughing, everyone thought it was really funny. But I actually had to leave the room. I just felt really bad. And I still feel really bad about it.
<v Elna Baker>我是很糟糕。她读出来时——全家人都在笑，每个人都觉得这很好笑。但我必须离开房间。我真的觉得很难受。到现在我对那件事依然感觉很糟糕。

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:47.620
<v Ira Glass>Some regrets just never go away, you know. People tell us that they forgive us. We try to forgive ourselves. And we still know, we did wrong. We hurt somebody. It was real. And that feeling, it can immobilize you. If you're lucky, it teaches you something that you take into other situations.
<v Ira Glass>有些悔恨是永远不会消散的，你知道的。人们告诉我们他们原谅了我们。我们试着原谅自己。但我们依然知道，我们做错了。我们伤害了别人。这是真实的。那种感觉会让你感到瘫痪。如果你足够幸运，它会教会你一些带入到其他境遇中的东西。

00:13:47.620 --> 00:14:00.200
<v Ira Glass>But I think, often, it's just like this pebble in your shoe that teaches you nothing. It doesn't slow you down, really. It just hurts. It just hurts in this way that does not stop hurting.
<v Ira Glass>但我认为，通常它就像鞋里的一颗鹅卵石，什么也教不了你。它真的不会拖慢你的脚步。它只会痛。它会以一种不会停止疼痛的方式一直痛着。

